<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n18263" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">flābellum</span></b> , i, n.
		dim.
		flabrum, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>a smali fan</i> or <i>fly-flap.</i>
		</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<b>Lit.</b>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">cape hoc flabellum, et ventulum huic sic
					facito,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Ter.
					Eun. 3, 5, 47</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">50</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Mart. 3, 82, 10</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">for this a peacock's tail was used,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Prop.
					2, 24</span></i>
			 (3, 18), 11; <i><span class="en">Hier. Ep. 27,
			13</span></i>.—* </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<b>Trop.</b>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">cujus lingua quasi flabello seditionis, illa
					tum est egentium concio ventilata,</span>”
				<i>an exciter</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Cic. Fl. 23, 54</span></i>
			.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
    <div class="alpheios-lex-alph-source">From <u>
            <u>A Latin Dictionary</u>
        </u> (Charlton T. Lewis, Charles Short, Oxford, Clarendon Press, 1879) </div>
